## Step 6 — Buyer Spec Audit

### Phase 1 — Top 2 RFQ Specs

Provided buyer specs: Ventilation, Capacity, Frame Material

**Ventilation** (Exhaust Fan / Air Purifier / Louvered Walls / Open Mesh Roof): Directly determines whether the cabin can be installed in the buyer's context (indoor airport terminal requires ducted exhaust or HEPA purifier; outdoor factory area may accept louvered walls). Sellers need this to confirm product fit and quote accurately. **Rank 1.**

**Capacity** (2–3 / 4–6 / 8–10 / 10–12 Person): Defines the scale of the structure — non-interchangeable. Sellers need this to identify the correct model and quote the right price. **Rank 2.**

*Why not Frame Material at Rank 2?* Frame Material (Aluminium / MS / Stainless Steel) is a quality/durability preference that is often resolved post-connection through negotiation. Capacity is a hard requirement — a seller cannot respond accurately without knowing how many people the cabin must accommodate. Capacity is more fundamental.

